# Testing & Quality Gates

## Two levels
**Partial** — on every PR from a work branch into `develop` (fast, < ~10 min):
lint · typecheck · unit tests · build · secret scan (gitleaks) · dependency audit (high/critical) · commitlint.

**Full** — on `develop` after merge, on PR `develop → staging`, on `staging`, and on PR `staging → main`:
everything in Partial **plus all of the following**.

### Functional testing
| Type | Tool (default) | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| Unit | Jest/Vitest · pytest | business rules, utils, services |
| Integration | Testcontainers / CI services (Postgres + Redis) | API endpoints against a real DB |
| Contract / API | OpenAPI schema validation (schemathesis / dredd-style) | API matches the published contract |
| End-to-end (E2E) | **Playwright** (web) · **Maestro** or Detox (mobile) | critical user journeys on a deployed environment |
| Regression | the E2E + integration suites | every bug fix adds a reproducing test |
| Smoke | Playwright tagged `@smoke` | after each deploy |
| Tenant isolation | integration | tenant A cannot touch tenant B — every tenant endpoint |
| UAT | checklist in the promotion PR | client/CTO sign-off before `main` |

### Non-functional testing
| Type | Tool (default) | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| Performance (web) | **Lighthouse CI** | Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices, SEO ≥ 90 on key pages (mobile) |
| Load / stress | **k6** | smoke load on develop/staging; full load before `main`: p95 < 500ms at expected peak, error rate < 1% |
| Security — SAST | CodeQL / Semgrep | no high/critical |
| Security — DAST | **OWASP ZAP** baseline against staging | no high alerts |
| Dependencies / supply chain | npm/pnpm audit, pip-audit, OSV-Scanner | no known high/critical vulns |
| Secrets | gitleaks | none |
| Accessibility | axe-core via Playwright | zero serious/critical violations (IS 5568 / WCAG 2.1 AA) |
| Visual regression | Playwright screenshots | no unapproved diffs |
| Compatibility | Playwright projects: Chromium, WebKit, Firefox + mobile viewports; EAS builds on iOS + Android | all pass |
| Resilience | tests for timeouts/retries of external services (Meta, AI, payments) | graceful degradation |
| SEO technical | sitemap/robots/canonical/structured-data checks | valid |

## Gates (enforced by branch protection — red = cannot merge)
| Gate | Required |
|---|---|
| PR → `develop` | Partial |
| PR `develop → staging` | Full on `develop` environment, green |
| PR `staging → main` | Full on `staging` + full load test + UAT + security review |
| After prod deploy | Smoke on production; watch errors 30 min; roll back on failure |

## Writing tests
- Arrange/Act/Assert; one behavior per test; descriptive names.
- Factories for test data; each test creates its own tenant. No real external calls (Meta, AI, payments) in
  unit/integration — fakes or recorded fixtures. E2E uses `data-testid`, never translated text.
- New/changed code ≥ 80% line coverage; every bug fix ships with a failing-first test.
- Flaky test = bug: quarantine with an issue and fix within the sprint. Never `.skip` to get green.
- Test plan per project in `docs/testing/TEST-PLAN.md` (skill: `full-test-suite`).
